        "target": "Given the problem, I identified the following quantities and the unknown:\n- Original price of a t-shirt: $20\n- Discount: 50%\n- Number of friends: 4\n- Unknown: Total amount spent by all friends\n\nTo solve this, I first calculated the discounted price of one t-shirt:\n- Discounted price = Original price * (1 - Discount)\n- Discounted price = $20 * (1 - 0.50) = $20 * 0.50 = $10\n\nNext, I calculated the total amount spent by all four friends:\n- Total amount = Discounted price * Number of friends\n- Total amount = $10 * 4 = $40\n\nTo verify the result, I checked the calculation by ensuring that the total amount spent ($40) is indeed the sum of the discounted prices of the t-shirts each friend bought. Since each friend bought one t-shirt at $10, and there are four friends, the total is $40.\n\nThe operations I used are straightforward and reusable for similar problems involving discounts and total cost calculations. I would reuse the operation of calculating the discounted price and then multiplying by the number of items purchased to find the total cost.\n\nFINAL: 40",
