        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "c7cbe033b31e8fdd5f72c85ddc26078b7467ad8b349554cff481d9de16031077",
        "target": "Given:\n- $5 per vampire\n- $10 per werewolf\n- Removed half the vampires\n- Removed 8 werewolves\n- Total earnings: $105\n- 4 times as many werewolves as vampires\n\nLet \\( v \\) be the number of vampires and \\( w \\) be the number of werewolves. We know \\( w = 4v \\).\n\nEarnings equation:\n\\[ 5 \\left(\\frac{v}{2}\\right) + 10 \\cdot 8 = 105 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{5v}{2} + 80 = 105 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{5v}{2} = 25 \\]\n\\[ 5v = 50 \\]\n\\[ v = 10 \\]\n\nSo, \\( w = 4 \\times 10 = 40 \\).\n\nHe removed 8 werewolves out of 40, so the percentage removed is:\n\\[ \\frac{8}{40} \\times 100 = 20\\% \\]\n\nFINAL: 20",
