        "target": "Given the problem, I identified the following quantities and relationships:\n- Van Helsing earns $5 per vampire and $10 per werewolf.\n- He removed half the vampires and 8 werewolves.\n- His total earnings were $105.\n- There were 4 times as many werewolves as vampires.\n\nFrom these, I defined:\n- \\( v \\) as the number of vampires.\n- \\( w \\) as the number of werewolves, with \\( w = 4v \\).\n\nI then set up the equation based on his earnings:\n\\[ 5 \\left(\\frac{v}{2}\\right) + 10 \\cdot 8 = 105 \\]\n\nSimplifying the equation:\n\\[ \\frac{5v}{2} + 80 = 105 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{5v}{2} = 25 \\]\n\\[ 5v = 50 \\]\n\\[ v = 10 \\]\n\nUsing \\( v = 10 \\), I calculated the number of werewolves:\n\\[ w = 4 \\times 10 = 40 \\]\n\nNext, I verified the number of werewolves removed:\n- He removed 8 werewolves out of 40.\n- The percentage removed is:\n\\[ \\frac{8}{40} \\times 100 = 20\\% \\]\n\nTo check the result, I recalculated his earnings:\n- Earnings from vampires: \\( 5 \\times \\frac{10}{2} = 25 \\)\n- Earnings from werewolves: \\( 10 \\times 8 = 80 \\)\n- Total earnings: \\( 25 + 80 = 105 \\)\n\nThis matches the given total earnings, confirming the solution is correct.\n\nFINAL: 20",
