{"gold":[{"independent_answer":"24 seeds are planted; the number of trees is not determined","question_sha256":"656efa5526605131797250a8d56a808049d4a95e90e9cfb59909577608d45fbf","reason":"There are 2 × 20 × 1 = 40 seeds, and 60% of 40 is 24 planted seeds. The question does not state that every planted seed is itself a planted tree or becomes one, so the gold 24 requires a questionable seeds-to-trees assumption.","status":"AMBIGUOUS","task_id":"gsm8k-train-171"},{"independent_answer":"84","question_sha256":"f347bdf8a2881955301849cb288691f9fab28335ae24d5c98c93ab1df232934b","reason":"One Dark CD costs 2 × 12 = 24 dollars. Two Dark CDs plus the AVN CD cost 2 × 24 + 12 = 60 dollars. The five 90s CDs cost 0.40 × 60 = 24 dollars, so the total is 60 + 24 = 84, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-6066"},{"independent_answer":"102","question_sha256":"ca016e8ee283ed8b0f3d2bde59e12d82352955ad164a84fc7f8e340d79f67149","reason":"The weekly charge is 2 × 10 + 1 × 5 = 25 dollars, hence four weeks cost 100 dollars. After the 18% discount the charge is 100 × 0.82 = 82 dollars; adding the 20-dollar fine gives 102, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-4715"},{"independent_answer":"45","question_sha256":"2fd74f61471da7f596641422ba375e5317d95b7f00aa5aa4ef99025dd722b3be","reason":"Six tickets and entrées cost 6 × (50 + 10) = 360 dollars. Half of six is three, so drinks cost 3 × 30 = 90 dollars. The group paid 450 dollars and lost the unrefunded 10%, or 0.10 × 450 = 45, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-2190"},{"independent_answer":"40","question_sha256":"9442490708eb891e8cf3e99d81109e1f611b8b7a1a90c4705783cd313dc2dd7d","reason":"A 50% discount makes each 20-dollar shirt cost 20 × 0.50 = 10 dollars. Four shirts cost 4 × 10 = 40, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1005"},{"independent_answer":"20","question_sha256":"1c0123ea27f99f47a723a1f5d87904a4950436222ebed952f922d0b1d83440aa","reason":"The